---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ZigCompat from '../components/ZigCompat.astro';
import CopyButton from '../components/CopyButton.astro';
import { ZIG } from '../data/versions';
---
<BaseLayout title="Getting Started - Zepplin Registry" active="docs">
  <div class="docs-container">
    <nav class="nav-breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/docs">Documentation</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span style="color: var(--text-primary);">Getting Started</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="docs-header">
      <h1 class="docs-title">Getting Started with Zepplin</h1>
      <p class="docs-subtitle">Set up Zepplin and start managing your Zig dependencies in minutes</p>
    </header>

    <div class="docs-content">
      <h2><span class="step-number">1</span>Prerequisites</h2>
      <p>Before you begin, ensure you have the following installed:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Zig {ZIG.dev}</strong> (master) - <a href="https://ziglang.org/download/">Download Zig</a></li>
        <li><strong>Git</strong> - For fetching packages from repositories</li>
        <li>A terminal/command prompt</li>
      </ul>

      <ZigCompat />


      <h2><span class="step-number">2</span>Adding Dependencies</h2>
      <h3>Option A: Using zig fetch (Recommended)</h3>
      <p>The easiest way to add a dependency is with <code class="inline-code">zig fetch --save</code>:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrap"><CopyButton code={`zig fetch --save https://github.com/user/package/archive/main.tar.gz\nzig fetch --save https://github.com/user/package/archive/refs/tags/v1.0.0.tar.gz`} /><div class="code-block"><code><span class="comment"># Add latest from main branch</span>
zig fetch --save https://github.com/user/package/archive/main.tar.gz

<span class="comment"># Or pin to a specific version tag (recommended for stability)</span>
zig fetch --save https://github.com/user/package/archive/refs/tags/v1.0.0.tar.gz</code></div></div>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">This automatically adds the dependency with its hash to your <code class="inline-code">build.zig.zon</code>.</p>

      <h3>Option B: Manual build.zig.zon Entry</h3>
      <p>You can also manually add dependencies to your <code class="inline-code">build.zig.zon</code>:</p>
      <div class="code-block"><code><span class="keyword">.dependencies</span> = .{'{'}
    <span class="keyword">.zqlite</span> = .{'{'}
        <span class="keyword">.url</span> = <span class="string">"https://github.com/ghostkellz/zqlite/archive/refs/tags/v1.5.4.tar.gz"</span>,
        <span class="keyword">.hash</span> = <span class="string">"1220abc123..."</span>, <span class="comment">// Get this from zig fetch output</span>
    {'}'},
{'}'},</code></div>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1rem; background: rgba(255,214,10,0.1); border-radius: 0.5rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--lightning-400);">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Always pin to a version tag (e.g., <code class="inline-code">refs/tags/v1.0.0</code>) for production projects. Using <code class="inline-code">main</code> or <code class="inline-code">master</code> branches can lead to unexpected breaking changes.
      </p>

      <h3>Option C: Clone and Build from Source</h3>
      <div class="code-block"><code><span class="comment"># Clone the repository</span>
git clone https://github.com/ghostkellz/zepplin.git
cd zepplin

<span class="comment"># Build the CLI tool</span>
zig build

<span class="comment"># The binary is in zig-out/bin/zepplin</span></code></div>

      <h2><span class="step-number">3</span>Initialize a Project</h2>
      <p>Create a new Zepplin project or initialize an existing Zig project:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrap"><CopyButton code="zepplin init" /><div class="code-block"><code>zepplin init</code></div></div>
      <p>This creates two files:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><code class="inline-code">zepplin.toml</code> - Your project configuration and dependencies</li>
        <li><code class="inline-code">zepplin.lock</code> - Lock file for reproducible builds</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="step-number">4</span>Add Dependencies</h2>
      <p>Add packages to your project using the <code class="inline-code">add</code> command:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrap"><CopyButton code={`zepplin add zig-clap\nzepplin add zap@0.3.0\nzepplin add mypackage --registry https://my-registry.example.com`} /><div class="code-block"><code><span class="comment"># Add a package (latest version)</span>
zepplin add zig-clap

<span class="comment"># Add a specific version</span>
zepplin add zap@0.3.0

<span class="comment"># Add from a custom registry</span>
zepplin add mypackage --registry https://my-registry.example.com</code></div></div>

      <h2><span class="step-number">5</span>Build Your Project</h2>
      <p>Build your project with all dependencies resolved:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrap"><CopyButton code="zepplin build" /><div class="code-block"><code>zepplin build</code></div></div>
      <p>This command resolves dependencies, downloads packages, and runs <code class="inline-code">zig build</code>.</p>

      <div class="note-box">
        <div class="note-box-title">Tip: Discover Packages</div>
        <p>Use the <code class="inline-code">discover</code> command to search for packages:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0;"><code>zepplin discover "http server"
zepplin trending
zepplin browse --category=cli</code></div>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="step-number">6</span>Publishing Packages</h2>
      <p>Ready to share your package? Make sure your <code class="inline-code">build.zig.zon</code> has the required fields:</p>
      <div class="code-block"><code><span class="keyword">.name</span> = <span class="string">"my-awesome-package"</span>,
<span class="keyword">.version</span> = <span class="string">"1.0.0"</span>,
<span class="keyword">.description</span> = <span class="string">"A brief description of your package"</span>,
<span class="keyword">.license</span> = <span class="string">"MIT"</span>,</code></div>
      <p>Then publish:</p>
      <div class="code-block-wrap"><CopyButton code={`zepplin login\nzepplin publish`} /><div class="code-block"><code><span class="comment"># Login to the registry (first time only)</span>
zepplin login

<span class="comment"># Publish your package</span>
zepplin publish</code></div></div>

      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/cli">CLI Reference</a> - Full command documentation</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/api">API Reference</a> - REST API documentation</li>
        <li><a href="/publish">Web Publishing</a> - Publish via the web interface</li>
        <li><a href="/docs/contribute">Contributing</a> - Help improve Zepplin</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .docs-container { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem; }
  .docs-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-bottom: 2rem; }
  .docs-title { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--lightning-400); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .docs-subtitle { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .docs-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .docs-content h2:first-child { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; margin-top: 0; }
  .docs-content h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .docs-content p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .docs-content ul, .docs-content ol { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-left: 1.5rem; }
  .docs-content li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .docs-content a { color: var(--lightning-400); }
  .code-block {
    background: var(--bg-tertiary); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem; font-family: 'Fira Code', 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 0.9rem; overflow-x: auto; margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .code-block code { color: var(--text-primary); white-space: pre; }
  .code-block .comment { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .code-block .keyword { color: var(--lightning-400); }
  .code-block .string { color: #a5d6ff; }
  .inline-code {
    background: var(--bg-tertiary); padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 0.25rem;
    font-family: 'Fira Code', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--lightning-400);
  }
  .note-box {
    background: rgba(255, 214, 10, 0.1); border: 1px solid var(--lightning-400);
    border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .note-box-title { font-weight: 600; color: var(--lightning-400); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .note-box p { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .nav-breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .nav-breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .nav-breadcrumb a:hover { color: var(--lightning-400); }
  .nav-breadcrumb span { color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0.5rem; }
  .step-number {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem; height: 2rem; background: var(--lightning-400); color: var(--bg-primary);
    border-radius: 50%; font-weight: 700; margin-right: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
